Let me reconsider: should validation run before or after the new snapshot gets recorded? 

Consider sequence:
• Session N starts: last snapshot = S(N-1), HEAD = H(N-1).
• Session N makes commits → HEAD = H(N).
• evolve calls `risk snapshot`: we want to validate S(N-1) against commits H(N-1)..H(N) — that's the outcome of session N's prediction. So validate FIRST (against current HEAD H(N)), THEN write S(N) at H(N). 

If we validated after writing S(N), `replay_validate_last_snapshot` would use S(N) (the just-written one) as "last" and git log S(N)..HEAD = empty (same hash), so it'd return None. So validation MUST run before writing the new snapshot. Order: validate → then snapshot. 

